    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Conservatives rely on a sophisticated theological framework that views life as an uncreated gift from God, making it an absolute good that cannot be forfeited by human will or medical intervention. They argue that MAiD fundamentally misplaces the source of value, shifting the definition of life from a divine mystery to a medical commodity subject to human control, which they see as a profound hubris. This perspective is grounded in the belief that the natural order of life and death is sacred and that altering it violates the very fabric of creation, regardless of the patient's suffering. Ultimately, they contend that true compassion lies in accepting the natural course of life rather than attempting to engineer an artificial end, which they view as a dangerous erosion of the human condition.",
