      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Liberal arguments do not simply discard the sanctity of life; rather, they redefine it as a dynamic process of flourishing that must end when suffering becomes unbearable and no longer serves the patient's dignity. They argue that true respect for life requires the moral courage to allow it to end naturally when the body can no longer sustain the person, rather than forcing a prolonged, painful existence that violates the patient's own will. This approach elevates autonomy and the relief of suffering as higher moral goods than the abstract concept of biological continuity, asserting that a life lived in agony is not a life worth preserving.",
